---
import PageLayout from '~/layouts/PageLayout.astro';
---
<PageLayout
  title="About"
  description="About Ken Tannenbaum and finnoybu.com — the personal home for his work in software, writing, publishing, and digital forensics."
>
  <article class="page-shell">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h1 class="page-title">Ken Tannenbaum</h1>

    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        finnoybu.com is where I keep my work in one place. The orbit on the
        front page is the map; this is the note behind it.
      </p>
      <p>
        I'm a software engineer. Alongside that I write, I publish, and I keep a
        handful of projects running across a few unrelated fields &mdash; AI
        governance, historical fiction, digital forensics, and a small
        publishing imprint among them. Some are professional and some are
        personal; a few were built quietly for specific people.
      </p>
      <p>
        What ties them together isn't a single subject. It's a way of working:
        take something that matters, build it properly, and see it through.
      </p>

      <h2>The name</h2>
      <p>
        "Finnoybu" comes from Finn&oslash;y, an island in the Stavanger channel
        on the southwestern coast of Norway, where my family's story begins. The
        name carries through the fiction, the family memoir, and the imprint, so
        it names the personal site too.
      </p>

      <h2>Elsewhere</h2>
      <p>
        Each project on the front page links out to its own home. To reach me
        directly, see the <a href="/contact">Contact</a> page.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</PageLayout>
